api.yaml; do not add extra role rules.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen for paths or HTTP methods that are not defined in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal 404/405 responses and add no undocumented operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If demo seed data cannot be written to PostgreSQL when Seed:Demo is true, how should startup behave?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup and surface the seed-write error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Should successful API writes remain available after the API process restarts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal PostgreSQL durability so successful writes remain available after an API restart.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 13 requirements be approved as one run, or should the work be split by cutting or deferring a part?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 13 requirements in one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should lot-list responses apply an additional authorizedYards restriction beyond the filtering and security rules declared in the API contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply only the lot-list filtering and security rules declared in contracts/openapi.yaml; add no authorizedYards restriction.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the profitability permission checks be covered for users with view and export permissions independently?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Add separate cases for the contract-defined view-only and export-only paths, checking their respective redaction and export-denial behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"After correcting or voiding a feeding event, how should the resulting stock be calculated when other persisted movements affect the same items?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Calculate stock using opening stock and all persisted receipts, adjustments, and feeding events, incorporating the correction or void.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement the Feedlot API exactly to the OpenAPI contract, with no undocumented operations or product-screen routes, and return contract-defined responses, errors, and security behavior.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide contract-defined sign-in, session, dashboard, and filtered lot-list behavior, without imposing an additional authorized-yards restriction on lot lists.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Implement procurement imports and allocation operations with contract-defined matching, PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen traceability, persisted quantities, and conflict results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Implement lot forecasts, forecast-setting updates, metrics, insights, planner actions, and weight-history operations with contract-defined values, calculations, suggestions, validation, and persisted updates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Implement inventory reads, writes, movements, projections, and CSV exports with contract-defined fields, calculations, validation, and persisted stock changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Implement ration reads, creation, revision, optimization, and approval with contract-defined data, calculations, and results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Implement feed-plan reads, creation, reviews, and status changes with contract-defined pen-level details, calculated quantities, audit state, and persisted status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Implement feeding-event reads, creation, correction, and voiding with contract-defined variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, and recalculated lot feed totals and stock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Implement operational, feed-to-gain, and profitability reports and exports with contract-defined filters, calculations, summaries, permissions, and artifacts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Implement sample-data status, loading, reset, and replacement operations, avoiding duplicate loads and requiring explicit confirmation for reset or replacement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Store contract domain data in the configured App PostgreSQL database, preserve writes across process restarts, and upgrade the schema without losing existing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, use SeedData.Run at startup to add 3 to 5 believable, contract-example-derived rows to each empty application table, leave nonempty tables unchanged, and fail startup while surfacing seed-write errors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, serve collection operations from persisted records, including empty collections when no records exist.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}